(At the time of writing, it remains unclear as to who is liable when )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(your bitcoin exchange is hacked or when the service shuts down )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(all of a sudden. Most of the bigger, more reputable exchanges have )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(systems in place that protect you from financial risk up to a certain )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(amount. The idea is that, if the exchange gets breached, or your )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(funds are lost in any other way while stored on the )Tj
/Span<</ActualText<FEFF00AD>>> BDC 
( )Tj
EMC 
23.4 0 Td
(platform, the )Tj
-23.4 -1.158 Td
(exchange will reimburse you out of its pocket. That said, we advise )Tj
T*
(you to take a sensible approach and only store on exchanges what )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(you need and not treat them as secure storage for\036your bitcoins.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Some economists would go as far as saying that a bitcoin exchange )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(is a self\037regulating platform, such as NASDAQ. However, as big )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(as the NASDAQ is, it claims immunity from computer crashes \227 )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(meaning it will not reimburse any funds lost due to a computer )Tj
-0.001 Tw 0 -1.158 TD
(crash. Bitcoin exchanges operate in a different manner, but with no )Tj
0 Tw 0 -1.158 TD
(clear regulator to report to, there is never a guarantee you will get )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(your money back.)Tj
-0.002 Tc 0 -2.316 TD
[(The amount of protection that exchanges may offer to customers)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(may well depend on where they are registered and the licensing)-2( )]TJ
T*
[(requirements \(or lack thereof\) for the exchanges to operate in that)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(jurisdiction. Storing your bitcoins on an exchange for more than a)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(day or two is never a good idea, and if that exchange were to cease)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(operating for any reason at all, your options will be determined by)-1.9( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(the local laws of the jurisdiction where the exchange is registered.)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(Generally speaking, the tougher the licensing requirements for an)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(exchange, the more protection you\222re likely to be offered. However,)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(you should verify the details of any exchange that you choose to)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(use and the level of protection that it may or may not offer you.)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(Granted, you may be able to take legal action should the worst)-2( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
(come to pass, but a lawsuit is very costly and time\037consuming.)Tj
0 Tc 0 -2.316 TD
(More and more bitcoin exchanges have opened the door to receive )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(independent third\037party audits. An auditor can verify whether a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bitcoin exchange is solvent enough to continue its operations, and )Tj
-0.001 Tw 0 -1.158 TD
(if needed, get the security measures stress\037tested to verify whether \)Tj
0 Tw 0 -1.158 TD
(or not user data is protected properly. We discuss current legisla)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(tive efforts in more details in Chapter\0369.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Every exchange has its own way of publishing audit results. To find )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(more information regarding the audit report of your preferred bit)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(coin exchange, contact its support via live chat or e-mail. A repre)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(sentative will be able to give you a clear answer on whether or not )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the company conducts audits and where the results are published.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Regardless of how you look at it, in the end, all liability lies with )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the people using bitcoin exchanges. Bitcoin puts financial con)Tj
