(The major focus of bitcoin and blockchain technology has always )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(been in terms of finances. And although bitcoin lets you send )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(money to anyone else in the world at little to no cost \227 and gives )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(you the ability to track this payment to the recipient \227 that may )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(not be ideal for everyone. This is why it is so important to keep )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(in mind that bitcoin is much more than a payment method. For )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(example, you can put the ownership of your car on the blockchain )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(and have it time-stamped by the network when the block associ)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ated with your data is confirmed. If you ever sell that car, you can )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(digitally transfer its ownership by sending it to anyone else on )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the bitcoin blockchain. And once that transfer has completed and )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(confirmed on the network, the new owner can officially lay claim )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(to that car. No paperwork needed \227 just the exchange of keys and )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the sending of the digital asset which represents the car.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Not every consumer wants to see his or her financial details )Tj
/Span<</ActualText<FEFF00AD>>> BDC 
0 -1.158 TD
( )Tj
EMC 
0 0 TD
(broadcasted on a public ledger for anyone to see. That is )Tj
/Span<</ActualText<FEFF00AD>>> BDC 
0 -1.158 TD
( )Tj
EMC 
0 0 TD
(completely understandable, but you have to keep in mind that )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(everyone is pseudonymous on the bitcoin network \227 there\222s )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(no reason to think that anyone else will find out who are you if )Tj
T*
(you don\222t want them to. Your )Tj
