(A short history of bitcoin mining)Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 Tc 9.5 0 0 9.5 99 411.7836 Tm
(Over the years, bitcoin mining has seen a tremendous evolution in )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(terms of the required hardware to mine bitcoins. Very little hard)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ware was required when bitcoin launched in 2009, as there was )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(little to no interest in the project. But as more and more people )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(caught wind of bitcoin and joined the network, the computational )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(power increased exponentially. The )Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(mining difficulty parameter)Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
( )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(\(which determines how much computation power is required )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(to solve the mathematical equations associated with generating )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bitcoins\) adjusted accordingly, in order to make sure new blocks )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(on the bitcoin network were still ten minutes apart. The reason )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(for keeping bitcoin blocks ten minutes apart is to collect as many )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(broadcasted bitcoin transactions into one block and validate these )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(transactions at the same time.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(In 2009, the first versions of the bitcoin client had a built\037in pro)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(cess that would let anyone running the software mine bitcoin with )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(their computer\222s central processing unit \(CPU\) \227 the main proces\)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(sor in a computer. Because every computer has a CPU, and only a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(handful of people were mining bitcoins at that time, there was very )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(little competition. In fact, most of the coins in the first few months )Tj
T*
(were mined by Satoshi Nakamoto, who also gave away some coins )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(to other people in order to allow testing of the bitcoin network.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(It didn\222t take long for one of the miners to figure out that the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(mining feature could be adapted to use a graphics processing )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(unit \(GPU\), rather than just a CPU. Because a GPU \227 also called a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(video card \227 is specifically designed to solve complex mathemati)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(cal tasks, it is able to mine bitcoin more efficiently than a CPU. )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(However, that performance is offset by a large increase in electric)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ity use, as GPUs draw a lot more power from the wall compared )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(to CPUs. This change was the first chapter in a long and storied )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bitcoin mining arms race.)Tj
