(Arrays \(FPGAs\) saw the light of day a few years ago, and they out)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(performed CPU mining by quite a margin. Furthermore, any FPGA )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(could mine nearly as fast as a GPU available at that time \227 while )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(using far less electricity to complete the task of mining bitcoins.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(When reading up on bitcoin mining these days, one term people )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(often come across is )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(ASIC,)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( which stands for )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(application\037specific )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(integrated circuit.)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( This is a microchip designed specifically to mine )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bitcoin. The first bitcoin ASICs started hitting the street in early )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(2013, and they outperformed GPU and FPGA mining by such a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(margin that miners scrambled to get their hands on one of these )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(shiny machines. But ASICs have a major downside as well: They )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(are very power hungry, they make a lot of noise, and they generate )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(a ton of heat. On the flipside, a bitcoin ASIC miner is vastly supe)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(rior to any other type of hardware in existence today and remains )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(quite costly in some cases.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(As these new devices started popping up, the need for electricity )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(increased exponentially. As a result, mining bitcoins is extremely )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(unprofitable in most parts of the world, unless you have access )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(to cheap or free electricity. In most cases, the investment cost )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(of bitcoin hardware, combined with the electricity costs, make it )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(impossible to make a profit by mining at home. But there is a solu)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(tion to that problem: Bitcoin )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(cloud mining)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( lets you mine bitcoin by )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(purchasing mining power from a machine hosted in a different part )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(of the world.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Cloud mining has become somewhat popular in recent years. It )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(allows you to mine without needing to buy and/or host the hard)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ware yourself. Most bitcoin cloud mining providers charge a daily )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(or monthly fee to cover electricity costs. Cloud mining allows a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(user to start earning money directly, rather than waiting on the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(delivery of some fancy machine. Chapter\03611 talks more about )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(cloud mining.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(In the future, as with all computer advancements, microchips )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(will be made smaller without sacrificing computational power. )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(And with smaller chips, more of them can be fitted onto a board, )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(increasing the machine\222s overall mining power. Engineers are )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(trying to reduce the energy use of these microchips too. Making )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(mining more energy efficient could lead to more profitability in )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(additional parts of the world.)Tj
