0 Tc 9.5 0 0 9.5 99 290.7836 Tm
(You could easily draw a parallel between online bitcoin wallet )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(providers and financial institutions such as banks. Both services )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(handle your personal funds, and you can check the balance, as )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(well as send and receive funds at any time. But you are trusting a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bank to keep your funds safe, and that\222s not what bitcoin is about. )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Ever since bitcoin\222s inception, trust has played an integral role in \)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the development of this ideology. We believe Satoshi Nakamoto )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(envisioned that the future development of bitcoin would eventu)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ally lead to a \223trustless\224 society, where all interactions were do\ne )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(between people directly, without using any third\036party service.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(An online bitcoin wallet service is very convenient, but it\222s also )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(a tremendous security risk. Being able to store bitcoins online )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(and accessing them from the browser at any time sounds like an )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(advantage, but in doing so, the user is relying on the online wallet )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(provider to be honest at all times.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Online wallet providers are third\036party services, as they will con)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(trol your funds for you. Additionally, the biggest security risk is )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(that, even though you know your online wallet address, you don\222t )Tj
T*
(have access to your private key. In the event of the online wallet )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(service shutting down or being hacked, you would have no control )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(over the funds being stored in your wallet.)Tj
