(If multiple inputs are associated with one bitcoin transaction, this )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(means that the amount being sent is coming from multiple bitcoin )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(wallet addresses. As mentioned in Chapter\0375, any bitcoin user can )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(generate an almost infinite amount of wallet addresses, each of )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(which can hold any amount of BTC.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Here\222s an example: If you send 2 BTC to lucky old \223Joe\224 again, \)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(1\037BTC comes from wallet address #2, 0.33 BTC comes from wallet )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(address #7, and the remainder comes from wallet address #8. In )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(this example, wallet addresses #1, #3, #4, #5, and #6 have no actual )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bitcoin balance and can therefore not be used as an input because )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(there is no unspent output associated with these addresses.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
