(The general rule about transactions is as follows: A bitcoin trans)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(action that has no confirmations on it will always be a high risk )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(for double\036spending. Briefly, a )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(double\037spend)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( means that a bitcoin )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(user can spend the amount of coins in a bitcoin wallet twice \(see )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Chapter\03710 for more on double\036spending\). In fact, any transaction\ )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(that has less than six confirmations on it carries the same risk. )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(However, merchant and payment processors are free to set their )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(own number of required confirmations. This rule does not apply )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(to bitcoin users who stick to bitcoin software on their computer )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(though, as funds will remain \223unconfirmed\224 until the six network )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(confirmations have been achieved. Mobile users, depending on )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(which wallet they choose, can spend incoming funds much faster.)Tj
