(Transaction priority is determined by a rather complicated math)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ematical formula. Priority is calculated as follows: It is the value\036\)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(weighted sum of input age \(how old the transaction is\) divided by )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the transaction size in bytes. For best measure, that weighted sum )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(should be above 57,600,000.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(As you may have guessed, sometimes there are more transactions )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(waiting to be broadcasted than can be included in the current )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(block. Any leftover transactions will remain in the miner\222s )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(memory )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(pool)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( \(a collection of transactions that have not yet been verified by )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the bitcoin network\), and will be included in future blocks, priori)Tj
