(As we\222ve mentioned, in contrast to credit card transactions, which )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(are subject to much higher fees than BTC transactions, bitcoin is )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(a non\036refundable payment method. That means that once a sender )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(sends funds from their wallet to a recipient, that transaction can\222t \)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(be reversed, and funds are gone for good.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Of course the recipient could send money back to the original )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(sender if need be. But a bitcoin payment cannot be cancelled )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(or charged back, unlike credit card transactions. The reason is )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(simple: Credit cards are issued by a central financial institution, )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(which can be called upon to request a refund. With bitcoin, there )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(is no central authority backing the digital currency, and users are )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(solely responsible for storing and sending BTC funds.)Tj
