9.5 0 0 9.5 99 575.2836 Tm
(There is no reason why bitcoin transactions should ever be made )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(subject to chargebacks either. Every bitcoin transaction is broad)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(casted on the blockchain, a public ledger collecting all BTC trans)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(fers from the past, present, and future \(see Chapter\0377 for more on )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the blockchain\). The blockchain makes it clear for everyone in the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(world to see where funds from \223address A\224 are being sent to and )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(for what amount.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Which brings us to another aspect of bitcoin and chargebacks that )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(is important to keep in mind. Whenever a customer sells bitcoin )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(to a customer, whether directly or through an exchange, it is key )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(never to use a reversible payment method. For example, if you\222re )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(selling BTC to Jonas, and he wants to pay for it in PayPal, the deal )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(should never go through. The reason for that is simple: Traditional )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(payment methods such as PayPal \()Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(www.paypal.com)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(\), Skrill )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(\()Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(www.skrill.com)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(\), and credit card transactions are subject to )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(fraud and chargebacks.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(PayPal is an especially annoying platform to use when selling )Tj
/Span<</ActualText<FEFF00AD>>> BDC 
0 -1.158 TD
( )Tj
EMC 
0 0 TD
(bitcoin, for multiple reasons. First of all, PayPal doesn\222t offer sel\ler )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(protection when dealing with \223digital goods.\224 Secondly, at the tim\e )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(of writing, bitcoin is still viewed as a \223digital good\224 by PayPal\222\s )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Terms of Service. Should the buyer request a refund through )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(PayPal, even after receiving the bitcoins, they will get their money )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(back, no questions asked. The same principle applies to Skrill )Tj
/Span<</ActualText<FEFF00AD>>> BDC 
0 -1.158 TD
( )Tj
EMC 
0 0 TD
(payments, even though all payments there are supposed to be )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(\223final.\224 Opening a dispute by the buyer will, most likely, lead to\ a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(refund by Skrill.)Tj
-0.003 Tw 0 -2.316 TD
(In either scenario, the seller has lost their bitcoins, because bitcoin \)Tj
0 Tw 0 -1.158 TD
(is a non\036refundable payment method and it can\222t be charged back.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Dealing with bitcoin is the end-user\222s personal responsibility \227 )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(something that should not be taken lightly. Being in full control of )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(personal finance at any given time is both a powerful feeling and a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(big responsibility.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Bitcoin merchants, on the other hand, see the benefit of )Tj
/Span<</ActualText<FEFF00AD>>> BDC 
( )Tj
EMC 
25.679 0 Td
(accepting )Tj
-25.679 -1.158 Td
(a payment method that is not subject to chargebacks. Fraud )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(through online payment methods is one of the biggest worries for )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(online retailers all around the world. Bitcoin can solve that prob)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(lem in its entirety. Additionally, accepting bitcoin can open the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(door to a new and larger customer base all around the world.)Tj
