(and Taxation)Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 Tc 9.5 0 0 9.5 99 468.7836 Tm
(Daniel Defoe famously wrote, \223Things as certain as death and )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(taxes, can be more firmly believed\224\037.\037.\037.\037often paraphras\ed as )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(\223Nothing is certain but death and taxes.\224 I can help you with the \)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(taxes element of bitcoin, but I\222m afraid you\222re on your own with )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the death bit.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Despite certain warnings issued by governments and central banks )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(regarding bitcoin and its disruptive nature \(see Chapter\0371 for more \)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(on that\), most countries are more than happy to allow digital cur)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(rency adoption for one simple reason: taxation.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Because digital currency can be seen as an income or wage, it can )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(be taxed. Additionally, using bitcoin to pay for goods and services )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(is taxable in certain countries as well. As long as the government )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(can make money from this \223new breed of electronic payments,\224 )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(there won\222t be much opposition.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Remember that the regulatory tax landscape could change at any )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(time, and it is always a good idea to check with your local govern)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ment as to how bitcoin can be used, and whether or not you have )Tj
T*
(to pay taxes on bitcoin. Countries such as Brazil, Canada, Finland, )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Bulgaria, and Denmark have issued taxation guidelines for bitcoin )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(usage, yet not all these guidelines are in effect at the time of pub)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(lication. Other countries, such as Belgium, Greece, Hong Kong, )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Japan, and New Zealand have no plans to tax bitcoin and other vir)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(tual currencies just yet.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Rest assured, though, that every individual country is looking )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(into bitcoin and the impact on that country\222s economy. Given the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(decentralized and potentially global nature of the product, it may )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(well be the case that broad regulations may have to be agreed )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(upon at a global level before some individual countries take the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(plunge of determining how to regulate bitcoin as a currency, or )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(even to treat it as a currency at all. As a practical example, many )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(countries have their own specific laws to cover anti\036money laun)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(dering and combatting the financing of terrorism \(AML/CFT\), )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(and these fall under the intergovernmental organization of the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Financial Action Task Force \(FATF\). It is possible that some inter)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(governmental steering will be required by some nations before )Tj
ET
