( Chapter\03710: Bitcoin Security)Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
20 0 0 20 356.82 615.6802 Tm
(137)Tj
-0.013 Tc -12.891 -2.45 Td
(The role of bitcoin nodes)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
0 Tc 9.5 0 0 9.5 99 548.1802 Tm
(Individual bitcoin users are not the only driving force in terms of )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(securing the bitcoin network. Over the past few years, dedicated )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bitcoin nodes have been added to the network with the sole pur)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(pose of receiving and broadcasting new bitcoin transactions to )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(other users and nodes on the network. Doing so takes the entire )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(decentralized aspect of bitcoin to a new level.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Every bitcoin )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(node)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( is a device \227 such as a computer, mobile )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(device, or even small devices such as a Raspberry Pi 2 \227 that )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(hosts the entire bitcoin blockchain since the genesis block was )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(created in 2009. The )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(genesis block)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( was the first block of data )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(on the bitcoin network, which awarded Satoshi Nakamoto with )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(50\036bitcoins. Ever since that time, bitcoin users have been able to )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(generate additional bitcoins and broadcast bitcoin transactions )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(throughout the world.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(A bitcoin node has the bitcoin client software installed, but does )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(not receive and transfer coins on its own accord, unless the node )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(owner decides differently. These nodes are simply additional )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(sources where the entire blockchain is stored to verify the integ)Tj
(-)Tj
T*
(rity, neutrality, and chronological order of all bitcoin transactions )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(between the genesis block and right now. \(See Chapter\0367 for more )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(on the blockchain.\))Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Running a bitcoin node does not reward the owner with additional )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bitcoins. The sole purpose of a bitcoin node is to strengthen the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(network. At the time of writing, there were more than 6,000 bitcoin )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(nodes in operation, with more being added all the time. To find )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(out more about the location of specific bitcoin nodes, visit the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Bitnodes website at )Tj
/T1_4 1 Tf
(https://getaddr.bitnodes.io/)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(.)Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
-0.015 Tc 24 0 0 24 60 188.1802 Tm
(Defending Bitcoin from Hackers)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
0 Tc 9.5 0 0 9.5 99 168.6802 Tm
(As mentioned earlier, the bitcoin network is a secure technol)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ogy that is unhackable by even the strongest computers or most )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(skilled hackers in the world. )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(Cryptography)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( \227 a technique for )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(secure communication in the presence of third parties, using long )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(sequences of unguessable secret codes \227 plays an important role )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(in bitcoin\222s security. Properly implemented, cryptography can )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(make a system extremely secure.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(In recent years, there has been a lot of confusion in mainstream )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(media regarding how bitcoin really works. Contrary to popular )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(belief, bitcoin is not run by a single person or authority, and )Tj
