(By providing hackers with a target in the form of one central point )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(of failure, shutting down a bitcoin service is far easier than attack)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ing the bitcoin network itself. Even if a bitcoin service is breached )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(by a hacker, there is no impact on the bitcoin network itself, as )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(these things are not linked to each other.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Bitcoin services use the blockchain to check and handle transac)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(tions, but they are not hooked into the blockchain itself. Some )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(people assume that if a bitcoin exchange is hacked, their connec)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(tion to the blockchain makes the bitcoin network itself vulnerable )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(as well. This is not the case, as bitcoin exchanges are services built )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(on top of the blockchain, albeit in a centralized manner.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(In fact, no direct connection exists between the bitcoin network )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(and any bitcoin service in existence today. The only connections )Tj
( )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(between users and the blockchain come from bitcoin wallets, )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(which are in a way layered on top of the blockchain itself as well. )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Direct interaction and alteration of the bitcoin blockchain is impos)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(sible for individual users, which is why an individual user getting )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(hacked does nothing to disrupt the bitcoin network at all. The )Tj
T*
(same principle applies to bitcoin services being hacked, as they )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(are a layer on top of the bitcoin network without having any direct )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(effect on the way the network works. All bitcoin services do is )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(broadcast certain types of transactions to the bitcoin network, but )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(if those transactions never get relayed, the bitcoin network will )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(continue working as before.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(At its core, the bitcoin network is unaffected by anything taking )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(place outside of its own direct reach. Only if the bitcoin network )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(were breached and altered by 51 percent or more would there be )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(a problem \(see the next section to find out why\). Given the current )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(computational processing power securing the network, obtaining )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(51 percent of that amount is next to impossible for any individual )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(or government.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
