9.5 0 0 9.5 99 575.2836 Tm
(confirmations the merchant waits for. For example, if the attacker )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(controls 10 percent of the network hashrate but the merchant )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(waits for 6 confirmations, the success probability is on the order of )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(0.1 percent.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(As described in a previous section, the )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(>50 percent attack)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(, on the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(other hand, will only succeed if the attacker controls more than )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(half of the network hashrate. Because the attacker can generate )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(blocks faster than the rest of the network, he can simply persevere )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(with his private fork until it becomes longer than the branch built )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(by the honest network, from whatever disadvantage. No amount of )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(transaction confirmations can prevent this attack.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(The biggest threat for merchants and bitcoin service providers is )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(a >50 percent attack, as that would indirectly make a brute force )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(attack a guaranteed success as well. Given the current amount of )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(computational power pointed at the bitcoin network, it seems very )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(unlikely such an attack will ever be pulled off successfully.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(One of the biggest issues with the bitcoin network is that there )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(are too many centralized services. Nearly every bitcoin exchange )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(and most bitcoin mining pools are centralized services. If a bitcoin )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(exchange gets hacked, it will not affect the blockchain itself, nor )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(open the door to double\037spend attacks. But when a large mining )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(pool gets hacked, the story could become quite different. Luckily )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(for everyone involved, currently there is no bitcoin mining pool )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(controlling half of the network. The largest mining pool owns )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(about 25 percent of the entire network\222s computational power. )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(However, even that percentage is sufficient to pull off a \223brute )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(force attack\224 in order to double\037spend bitcoins, should an attacke\r )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(decide to do so.)Tj
