(because there was next to no competition on the network. In fact, )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(during the first few weeks, there were only a handful of miners.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(It didn\222t take long for a bitcoin enthusiast to figure out the code t\o )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(let his graphics card do all the computational work, as graphics )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(cards are designed to do exactly that. Even when playing video )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(games, a graphics card is doing nothing more than processing )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(computational data over and over again, at a rapid pace.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(The difference in mining speed between CPU mining and GPU )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(mining is simply astonishing. Productivity increases exponentially, )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(and the first GPU miners started strengthening the bitcoin network )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(tenfold. Despite all that extra mining power, new blocks were still )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ten minutes apart, thanks to the change in mining difficulty.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(A few years ago, CPU and GPU mining became completely obso)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(lete when FPGAs came around. An )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(FPGA)Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
( is a Field Programmable )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(Gate Array, which can produce computational power similar to )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(most GPUs around 2013, while being far more energy\036efficient than )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(graphics cards. Needless to say, quite a few miners switched from )Tj
T*
(CPU mining to GPU mining and then to FPGA mining within a few )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(years.)Tj
-0.006 Tc 0 -2.316 TD
[(But the mining hardware business keeps evolving even now, and)-6( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
[(FPGAs were only useful for a short amount of time. Bitcoin ASICs)-6( )]TJ
-0.005 Tw 0 -1.158 TD
[(were introduced to the scene in 2013, and these Application\036Specific)-6( )]TJ
0 Tw 0 -1.158 TD
[(Integrated Circuits cut down electricity requirements even further,)-6( )]TJ
0 -1.158 TD
(while outperforming GPU and FPGA mining by quite a margin.)Tj
0 Tc 0 -2.316 TD
(That said, there are some downsides associated with bitcoin ASIC )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(mining. Although the energy consumption is far lower than graph)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(ics cards, the noise production goes up exponentially, as these )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(machines are far from quiet. Additionally, ASIC bitcoin miners )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(produce a ton of heat and are all air\036cooled, with temperatures )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(exceeding 150 degrees F.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Buying a bitcoin ASIC miner also involves some hefty shipping )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(fees \227 these machines are quite heavy. Plus, you are guaranteed )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(to pay import duty on a bitcoin ASIC shipment as well, due to the )Tj
T*
(size and weight. All in all, ASICs today are a very costly investment )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(with absolutely no guarantee of the customer ever breaking even, )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(let alone making a profit.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Last but not least, bitcoin ASICs can only produce so much compu)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(tational power until they hit an invisible wall. Most devices are not )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(capable of producing more than 1.5 TH/s \(terrahash\) of computa)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(tional power, forcing customers to buy these machines in bulk if )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(they want to start a somewhat serious bitcoin mining business.)Tj
