(It should come as no surprise to find out that most people have )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(moved away from bitcoin mining hardware themselves and )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(switched over to cloud mining \(even though there are a lot of risks )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(associated with bitcoin cloud mining companies, as most of them )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(are far from legitimate.\) And the low bitcoin price is not helping )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(matters either. See the earlier section on cloud mining to find out )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(about the measures you can take to protect yourself.)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
-0.013 Tc 20 0 0 20 99 474.2836 Tm
(Calculating your costs)Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 Tc 9.5 0 0 9.5 99 455.7836 Tm
(Regardless of whether you want to buy hardware or sign up for a )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(bitcoin cloud-mining contract, you need to do some homework to )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(determine costs, earnings, and the expected time until you receive )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(your investment back to start making a profit.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Bitcoin mining costs go far beyond the original investment in the )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(hardware, logistics costs, and import duty fees. One of the main )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(factors to keep in consideration is power usage, as electricity costs )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(fluctuate greatly from country to country.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(In most countries, the price per kilowatt hour \(kWh\) makes bitcoin )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(mining unprofitable. Make sure to check a recent electricity bill )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(and determine the price per kWh and then calculate how much )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(kWh your bitcoin mining hardware will use on a daily basis.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(For example, a bitcoin miner drawing 600 watts from the wall )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(will consume 12.4 kWh per day. Calculations for this are simple: )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(600W )Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(\327)Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
( 24 hours in a day = 12,400W or 12.4 kWh. If you pay )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
($0.10\037per\037kWh, your daily electricity bill will be $1.24.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(This cost has to be weighed against the daily income you can earn )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(from bitcoin mining. These daily earnings will heavily depend on )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(the current bitcoin price, which is fairly low at the time of writing. )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(A higher bitcoin price would drastically improve earnings, while )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(electricity costs remain the same \(unless your supplier decides to )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(make a price change\).)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(Electricity is not the only cost. Owning bitcoin mining hardware )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(means maintaining it at all times and repairing it if something )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(breaks down. Some bitcoin ASIC miners don\222t come with a power )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(supply, which you have to purchase as well.)Tj
0 -2.316 TD
(The biggest and most important cost is investing time and effort to )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(optimize mining earnings. Most bitcoin mining hardware will per)Tj
(-)Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(form at its highest rate out of the box, but there are always tweaks )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(that can be made. Most manufacturers release new firmware )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(for the mining hardware at regular intervals to fix any bugs and )Tj
0 -1.158 TD
(squeeze out that extra bit of computational power.)Tj
